 answer."],["Read the answer","Each event shows its section, how many outlets in how many countries reported it and ATHENA's risk score. Open it to see who reported it first, every report in order and the reasons behind the score."]],"tips":["Headlines stay in English as the outlets published them, so headline words match best in English; places, trackers, sections and periods work in every language.","Ask searches the events published on this site — the most important of recent weeks — not every article ATHENA has read.","Risk is ATHENA's estimate from 0 to 10 of the harm described in the reporting, with its confidence. It is not a forecast and not advice."],"private":"Your question never leaves your browser: it is matched against the events published on this site. Nothing is sent or stored.","mm":{"head":"How this answer was made","scope":"Ask searches the events published on this site; each event page stays online for 14 days. An event is published only when at least 2 independent outlets have reported it within 48 hours, its importance is at least 3 and it has a clear category. Copies of one agency report count once.","read":"Your question was read in your browser by fixed word lists and rules. No generative AI is used and nothing was sent anywhere. Words that were not recognised are searched for in the headlines.","country":"Country: {v}. An event matches when the country is named in its reports.","region":"Region: {v}. An event matches when it names at least one country of that region.","topic":"Tracker: {v}. An event matches when ATHENA has assigned it to that risk tracker.","section":"Section: {v}. Events filed under that section match.","since":"Period: {v}, counted from the last time the event was reported.","risk":"Risk {v} or higher: only events with a risk score of at least {v} match.","rmax":"Risk under {v}: only events with a risk score below {v} match.","words":"Words: {v}. They are searched for in the headlines, which stay in English as the outlets published them.","sort_latest":"Order: newest first, by the time the event was last reported.","sort_covered":"Order: most widely reported first, by the number of countries and then of outlets.","sort_risk":"Order: highest risk first, then by importance.","sort_rel":"Order: best match first. Words in the headline and the countries asked for count most, then importance, with a small advantage for events reported in the last 24 hours.","scale":"Risk is ATHENA's estimate, from 0 to 10, of how severe and urgent the harm described is: 4 or more is elevated, 6 or more high, 8 or more critical. Each event page lists the reasons behind its score.","count":"{n} of the {m} events on the site match.","data":"Events as published on {gen}.","limits":"Scores describe news coverage, not facts on the ground, forecasts or probabilities. Sources are English-language, and places and topics are detected automatically and can occasionally be wrong. The methods are provisional and transparent.","help":"This answer is the site's own help text for your question, with a link to the page it describes. It was picked by matching your words to the key words of the question; no news data was used."}},"sheet":{"title":"Answer sheet","sub":"ATHENA Glaux Ask - an answer from the events published on this site, with its method and fingerprints.","q":"Question","when":"Made","when_note":"From the events published on this site, last updated {gen}.","page":"Page address","read":"How ATHENA read the question","answers":"Events found","risk":"Risk","outlets":"Outlets","countries":"Countries","more":"{n} more events match; open the page to see them all.","none":"No event on the site matches all of that.","meth":"Method","meth_rules":"The question is read in the reader's browser: places, trackers, sections, periods and risk levels are recognised from fixed word lists, and the events published on this site are filtered and ordered by them. No model guesses the answer, and nothing about the question was sent anywhere.","integ":"Fingerprints (SHA-256)","chash":"Content of this sheet (question, reading, answers)","dhash":"The published event data used","gen":"updated","vhash":"The word lists used (Ask vocabulary)","btc":"Bitcoin timestamps","btc_day":"ATHENA timestamps its records on the Bitcoin blockchain every day; the proofs are published at {u}.","btc_own":"This sheet was also stamped on Bitcoin when it was made. The stamp file (.ots) comes in the same download as this PDF. It stays pending until Bitcoin confirms it, usually within hours.","btc_none":"This sheet carries no Bitcoin stamp of its own.","limits":"A timestamp shows only that the sheet existed no later than the Bitcoin block that records it. It does not show that the answers are true. Risk is ATHENA's estimate from 0 to 10, not a forecast and not advice.","btn_pdf":"Answer sheet (PDF)","btn_stamp":"PDF with Bitcoin stamp","stamping":"Stamping on Bitcoin...","done":"The sheet was saved to your downloads.","done_stamp":"Saved: PDF, Bitcoin stamp (.ots) and read-me in one ZIP. Stamped through {cals}.","failed":"The sheet could not be made. Please try again.","stamp_failed":"The Bitcoin calendars did not answer. Nothing was saved; try again, or take the PDF without a stamp.","stamp_note":"The stamp sends only the PDF's 32-byte fingerprint to public OpenTimestamps servers - never your question or the answers.","readme":"ATHENA Glaux - answer sheet with Bitcoin stamp\r\n\r\nFiles\r\n  {pdf}      the answer sheet\r\n  {pdf}.ots  its Bitcoin timestamp (OpenTimestamps)\r\n\r\nSHA-256 of the PDF: {hash}\r\nStamped: {time}, through {cals}\r\n\r\nHow to check it\r\n  1. Open https://opentimestamps.org\r\n  2. Drop the .ots file, then the PDF, on the page.\r\n  3. Right after stamping the status is pending; Bitcoin confirms it within hours. Check again later; the site completes the proof.\r\n\r\nWhat it proves: the PDF existed no later than the Bitcoin block that records the stamp. It does not prove the answers are true.\r\n"},"help":[{"id":"follow","q":"How do I follow a country, a section or a tracker?","a":"Press ☆ Follow on any country, section, tracker or story. The front page then shows \"For you\" with the latest stories about what you follow. It is free and kept only in your browser.","href":"alerts.html","s":["follow","followed","following","subscribe","watchlist"],"w":["save","track"]},{"id":"alerts","q":"How do I get alerts on Telegram or X?","a":"Join the ATHENA group on Telegram or follow @athenaglauxinte on X - the buttons are at the bottom of every page. On the site, follow what you need with ☆ Follow.","href":"alerts.html","s":["alert","alerts","notification","notifications","notify","telegram","twitter"],"w":["x"]},{"id":"risk","q":"What does the risk score mean?","a":"Risk (0-10) is ATHENA's measure of how serious the harm in the reports is, how far it reaches and how urgent it is. 6 or more is high, 8 or more critical. The reasons behind every score are on the event's page.","href":"how.html","s":[],"w":["rated","rating","risk","score","scores","scoring"]},{"id":"confidence","q":"What does confidence mean?","a":"Confidence is how sure ATHENA is that the event happened as reported: how many independent outlets report it, how reliable they are and whether their accounts agree.","href":"how.html","s":["confidence"],"w":["certain","certainty","reliability","reliable","sure"]},{"id":"verified","q":"How does ATHENA check that a story is real?","a":"An event appears only when at least two independent outlets report it. Each event lists every report, who was first and from which countries, with links to the originals.","href":"how.html","s":["checked","fake","verification","verified","verify"],"w":["outlets","real","sources","true"]},{"id":"ask","q":"How do I search with Ask?","a":"Type what you want in your own words: a country, a region, a section, a tracker, a period or a level of risk - for example \"Greece this week\", \"Red Sea shipping\" or \"risk 7+\".","href":"ask.html","s":["examples","find","search","searching"],"w":["ask","query"]},{"id":"language","q":"How do I change the language?","a":"Use the language menu with the flag at the top of every page. ATHENA is in English, Greek and French; headlines are shown as the outlets published them.","href":"","s":["language","languages","translate","translation"],"w":[]},{"id":"look","q":"How do I make the text bigger or switch to dark mode?","a":"At the top of every page, A− A A+ change the text size and the palette button switches the look: classic, night, Aegean, future, neon or high contrast. Your choice is remembered in this browser.","href":"","s":["bigger","colors","colours","contrast","dark","font","mode","night","size","smaller","theme"],"w":["look","text"]},{"id":"countries","q":"Where do I see the news of one country?","a":"Open World at the top and choose a continent, or open Countries: every country in the news has its own page with its events, its risk and its last 30 days.","href":"countries.html","s":["countries","country","nation"],"w":["local"]},{"id":"maritime","q":"Where are shipping and the chokepoints?","a":"Maritime & Shipping shows the world's chokepoints and major ports with their status today, the incidents of the last 72 hours and the official notices in force.","href":"maritime.html","s":["chokepoint","chokepoints","maritime","navtex","ports","shipping","ships"],"w":["sea"]},{"id":"trackers","q":"What are the risk trackers?","a":"Trackers follow one situation over time - the Strait of Hormuz, the Red Sea, Greece-Turkey, Ukraine and more - with the risk now, its trend and the latest events.","href":"topics.html","s":["hotspot","hotspots","tracker","trackers"],"w":["situation","trend"]},{"id":"about","q":"Is ATHENA free, and who makes it?","a":"ATHENA Glaux is free, with no sign-up and no tracking cookies. It is an automated news-intelligence service, not a newspaper; the About page explains who makes it and how.","href":"about.html","s":["about","accou